IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa25-names-ch2`

-- coa25-tests-names-ch2.l4: tests for coa25-names-ch2.l4 (ss 1200 to 1208).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section and written down before the run.

-- The penalty these sections state, written out by hand from the text: level 3 and one-tenth of level 3.
`s 1203 test penalty level 3 with a tenth` MEANS
    Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                 `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                 `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                 `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                 `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- ---- s 1200(1) (arguments: the kind of person; carries on business in the United Kingdom under a business name)
#ASSERT `s 1200(1) the person is a person to whom this Chapter applies` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1200(1) the person is a person to whom this Chapter applies` `s 1200 a partnership` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1200(1) the person is a person to whom this Chapter applies` `s 1200 an individual` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not carrying on business under a business name
#ASSERT `s 1200(1) the person is a person to whom this Chapter applies` `s 1200 a partnership` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1200(1) the person is a person to whom this Chapter applies` `s 1200 another kind of person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a company is neither

-- ---- s 1200(3): the permitted additions (arguments: the kind of person; the addition)
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 an individual` `s 1200 an individual's forename or initial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 a partnership` `s 1200 an individual's forename or initial` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 a partnership` `s 1200 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 an individual` `s 1200 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 a partnership` `s 1200 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 an individual` `s 1200 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 an individual` `s 1200 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 a partnership` `s 1200 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 another kind of person` `s 1200 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 an individual` `s 1200 any other addition` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` `s 1200 a partnership` `s 1200 any other addition` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1200(2): "business name" (arguments: the kind of person; the name consists of the surname or surnames; the additions)
#ASSERT `s 1200(2) the name is a business name` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE -- his surname, no addition: not a business name
#ASSERT `s 1200(2) the name is a business name` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE (LIST `s 1200 an individual's forename or initial`) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- surname with a forename: not a business name
#ASSERT `s 1200(2) the name is a business name` `s 1200 a partnership` TRUE (LIST `s 1200 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames`, `s 1200 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1200(2) the name is a business name` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE (LIST `s 1200 any other addition`) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an addition other than a permitted addition: a business name
#ASSERT `s 1200(2) the name is a business name` `s 1200 an individual` FALSE EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a name other than the surname
#ASSERT `s 1200(2) the name is a business name` `s 1200 a partnership` TRUE (LIST `s 1200 an individual's forename or initial`) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) is for an individual
#ASSERT `s 1200(2) the name is a business name` `s 1200 another kind of person` TRUE EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1201(1) (arguments: the kind of person; the name or names stated; an address for each person named)
#ASSERT `s 1201(1) the disclosure contains the information required by this Chapter` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1201(1) the disclosure contains the information required by this Chapter` `s 1200 a partnership` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1201(1) the disclosure contains the information required by this Chapter` `s 1200 a partnership` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not the name of each member
#ASSERT `s 1201(1) the disclosure contains the information required by this Chapter` `s 1200 an individual` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no address for service
#ASSERT `s 1201(1) the disclosure contains the information required by this Chapter` `s 1200 another kind of person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) (arguments: a place of business in the United Kingdom; the address is in the United Kingdom)
#ASSERT `s 1201(2) the address meets the requirement as to place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1201(2) the address meets the requirement as to place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1201(2) the address meets the requirement as to place` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no place of business in the United Kingdom: (2) does not engage
-- (3) (arguments: a place of business in the United Kingdom; physical delivery; acknowledgement of delivery)
#ASSERT `s 1201(3) the address meets the requirement as to delivery` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1201(3) the address meets the requirement as to delivery` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1201(3) the address meets the requirement as to delivery` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1201(3) the address meets the requirement as to delivery` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a place of business in the United Kingdom: (3) does not engage

-- ---- s 1202(1) (arguments: the kind of document; the s 1203(1) answer)
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` `s 1202 a business letter` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` `s 1202 a written order for goods or services to be supplied to the business` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` `s 1202 an invoice or receipt issued in the course of the business` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` `s 1202 a written demand for payment of a debt arising in the course of the business` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` `s 1202 another document` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- list not closed
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` `s 1202 a business letter` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- exempt under s 1203
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` `s 1202 a business letter` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the exemption's conditions are not met
-- (arguments: the requirement applies; the information is stated; in legible characters)
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not legible
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not apply
#ASSERT `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) (arguments: someone has asked; immediately given; by written notice)
#ASSERT `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not immediately
#ASSERT `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not by written notice
#ASSERT `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- nobody asked

-- ---- s 1203(2) (arguments: the list is maintained; no partner's name appears except in the text or as a signatory; the document states the address and that the list is open to inspection)
#ASSERT `s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (c)
-- ---- s 1203(1): "a partnership of more than 20 persons" (arguments: the number of persons; the (2) answer)
#ASSERT `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` 21 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 21 is more than 20
#ASSERT `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` 20 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 20 is not more than 20
#ASSERT `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` 100 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` 21 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the conditions are not met
#ASSERT `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` 21 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ---- s 1203(3) (arguments: a list is maintained for the purposes of s 1203; during office hours)
#ASSERT `s 1203(3) the person may inspect the list` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1203(3) the person may inspect the list` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not during office hours
#ASSERT `s 1203(3) the person may inspect the list` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no list is maintained: the "Where" fails
-- ---- s 1203(4) (arguments: an inspection required in accordance with s 1203 was refused; the member refused it or permitted it to be refused; reasonable excuse)
#ASSERT `s 1203(4) the member of the partnership commits an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1203(4) the member of the partnership commits an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "without reasonable excuse"
#ASSERT `s 1203(4) the member of the partnership commits an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a member who did not refuse or permit the refusal
#ASSERT `s 1203(4) the member of the partnership commits an offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no inspection was refused
#ASSERT `s 1203(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1203` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 1203 test penalty level 3 with a tenth`
#ASSERT `s 1203(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1203` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1203(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1203` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1204(1) (arguments: premises where the business is carried on; customers or suppliers have access)
#ASSERT `s 1204(1) the requirement to display the notice applies to the premises` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1204(1) the requirement to display the notice applies to the premises` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not premises where the business is carried on
#ASSERT `s 1204(1) the requirement to display the notice applies to the premises` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1204(1) the requirement to display the notice applies to the premises` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no access for customers or suppliers; limb (b) is a condition of the same "in any premises" clause as limb (a), and the function asks whether the requirement applies, so a failed condition is JUST FALSE (fork F24)
-- (arguments: the requirement applies; a notice is displayed in a prominent position)
#ASSERT `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1205(1) (arguments: the s 1202(1) answer; the s 1202(2) answer; the s 1204(1) answer; a reasonable excuse)
#ASSERT `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- fails s 1202(1)
#ASSERT `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- fails s 1202(2)
#ASSERT `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- fails s 1204(1)
#ASSERT `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "without reasonable excuse"
#ASSERT `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no failure
#ASSERT `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- one failure is enough
#ASSERT `s 1205(2) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (arguments: the body commits the offence; the officer is in default)
#ASSERT `s 1205(2) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- an officer not in default: limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `s 1205(2) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1205(2) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the body committed no offence
#ASSERT `s 1205(2) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1205(3) the penalty for an offence under s 1205` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 1203 test penalty level 3 with a tenth`
#ASSERT `s 1205(3) the penalty for an offence under s 1205` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1205(3) the penalty for an offence under s 1205` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1205(4) the requirement is a requirement of s 1202 or s 1204` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1205(4) the requirement is a requirement of s 1202 or s 1204` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1206(1) (arguments: brought by a person to whom Chapter 2 applies to enforce a right under a contract; in breach of s 1202(1) or (2) or s 1204(1) when the contract was made)
#ASSERT `s 1206(1) this section applies to the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1206(1) this section applies to the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1206(1) this section applies to the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not in breach when the contract was made
-- (2) (arguments: the s 1206(1) answer; the defendant shows (a) an unpursuable claim; the defendant shows (b) financial loss; the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to continue)
#ASSERT `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless" the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable
#ASSERT `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the defendant shows neither
#ASSERT `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1206(3) the requirement is a requirement of this Chapter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1206(3) the requirement is a requirement of this Chapter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1206(4) the section affects the right to enforce rights against another person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1206(4) the section affects the right to enforce rights against another person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1207 (arguments: an offence under Part 41; the number of the section)
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` TRUE 1121 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` TRUE 1123 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` TRUE 1124 EQUALS NOTHING -- not among the sections named
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` TRUE 1125 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` TRUE 1131 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` TRUE 1132 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` TRUE 1120 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` FALSE 1121 EQUALS NOTHING -- not an offence under this Part

-- ---- s 1208
#ASSERT `s 1208 the activity is a business` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1208 the activity is a business` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1208 the abbreviation is an initial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1208 the abbreviation is an initial` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1208 the arrangement is a partnership` `s 1208 a partnership within the Partnership Act 1890` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1208 the arrangement is a partnership` `s 1208 a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1208 the arrangement is a partnership` `s 1208 a firm or entity of a similar character formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1208 the arrangement is a partnership` `s 1208 another arrangement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (arguments: a peer or a person usually known by a British title; the title by which he is known)
#ASSERT `s 1208 the surname of the person` TRUE "Lord Example" EQUALS JUST "Lord Example"
#ASSERT `s 1208 the surname of the person` FALSE "Lord Example" EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- the regulative rules, run with #TRACE. Expected values, decided from the text: the person does what is required: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 1202(1) the person must state the information on the document` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies` DOES `s 1202 state the information required by Chapter 2, in legible characters, on the document` AT 1
#TRACE `s 1202(2) the person must give the information to a person who asks` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies` DOES `s 1202 give the information required by Chapter 2, immediately and by written notice, to a person who asks` AT 1
#TRACE `s 1204(1) the person must display the notice in the premises` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies` DOES `s 1204 display a notice containing the information required by Chapter 2 in a prominent position in the premises` AT 1
